LOK: a media object's view makes no player

Painting a slide with a video under LOK built a hidden MediaWindow
on the document window, whose player (MFPlay on Windows) started
creating its media item. The paint's view went away, the player
with it, and MFPlay's queued creation callback then ran against
freed memory: the worker died, in 6 of 8 opens of a 60-slide deck
with one video (Ely R15.13a). A kit client plays media itself
(ElyShow natively); the slide shows the file's poster frame.
diff --git a/svx/source/sdr/contact/viewobjectcontactofsdrmediaobj.cxx b/svx/source/sdr/contact/viewobjectcontactofsdrmediaobj.cxx
